            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "High-Level Summary Technical Assistance Report\nFiscal Affairs Department"
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph_title",
            "bbox": [
                0.249,
                0.177,
                0.749,
                0.209
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "Workshop on Fraud and Investigations Involving Crypto Assets\nPrepared by Thomas Cantens"
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.112,
                0.235,
                0.836,
                0.282
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "The High-Level Summary Technical Assistance Report series provides high-level summaries of the assistance provided to IMF capacity development recipients, describing the high-level objectives, findings, and recommendations.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.112,
                0.293,
                0.881,
                0.441
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "ABSTRACT: In response to a request from the South African Revenue Service (SARS), the International Monetary Fund (IMF) conducted a capacity development workshop in November 2025 focused on fraud and investigations involving crypto assets. The workshop was the first of its kind. It aimed to enhance SARS' investigative and intelligence capabilities by providing technical knowledge on the crypto asset ecosystem, regulatory frameworks, and practical investigation techniques. Key findings highlighted the evolving regulatory environment in South Africa, the challenges posed by crypto assets for tax and customs enforcement, and the benefits of cross-agency collaboration and open-source intelligence tools. Recommendations emphasize the need for ongoing training tailored to different expertise levels, and the development of analytical and investigative tools to better detect and address crypto-related fraud and tax evasion.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.122,
                0.454,
                0.444,
                0.471
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "JEL Classification Numbers: K42, H26, F19",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.122,
                0.478,
                0.543,
                0.495
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "Keywords: crypto assets, financial investigations, training",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.112,
                0.675,
                0.882,
                0.755
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "The contents of this document constitute a high-level summary of technical advice provided by the staff of the International Monetary Fund (IMF) to the authorities of a member country or international agency (the \"CD recipient\") in response to their request for capacity development. Unless the CD recipient specifically objects within 30 business days of its transmittal, the IMF will publish this high-level summary on IMF.org (see Staff Operational Guidance on the Dissemination of Capacity Development Information).",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.322,
                0.78,
                0.675,
                0.872
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "International Monetary Fund, IMF Publications\nP.O. Box 92780, Washington, DC 20090, U.S.A.\nT. +(1) 202.623.7430 • F. +(1) 202.623.7201\npublications@IMF.org\nIMF.org/pubs",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
