    [
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.112,
                0.091,
                0.885,
                0.18
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "specialized teams and tools to trace crypto transactions, cooperate across agencies, and execute asset forfeiture procedures despite technical and jurisdictional challenges. Practical exercises during the workshop demonstrated the utility of open-source intelligence (OSINT) tools and commercial platforms for transaction tracing and fraud detection, highlighting the importance of combining technological knowledge with investigative rigor.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.111,
                0.186,
                0.876,
                0.276
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "Finally, the workshop fostered internal collaboration within SARS by bringing together diverse units with varying technical expertise. This cross-divisional interaction generated an internal dynamic, it helped identify knowledge gaps and establish internal points of contact for technical support, which is critical for addressing the multifaceted nature of crypto-related fraud that spans tax evasion and customs violations.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph_title",
            "bbox": [
                0.113,
                0.298,
                0.516,
                0.321
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "Summary of Recommendations"
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.112,
                0.332,
                0.868,
                0.386
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "This workshop being the first of its kind, the IMF and SARS teams dedicated time to draw some lessons from this exercise, which should be conducted again, internally and jointly with other revenue administrations and the IMF.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.112,
                0.392,
                0.877,
                0.501
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "To build on the workshop's achievements and address the challenges identified, capacity development efforts should focus on enhancing both technical knowledge and practical investigative skills. Training programs need to be tailored to different levels of expertise, ensuring that frontline officers receive sufficient technological grounding while technical specialists gain hands-on experience with investigative tools. As a lesson learnt, integrating practical exercises throughout training, rather than isolating technical content, will improve knowledge retention and operational effectiveness.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.112,
                0.506,
                0.876,
                0.614
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "Strengthening internal collaboration within revenue administration is essential to create a cohesive response to crypto asset-related fraud. This may include formalizing communication channels between tax, customs, data science, and specialized crypto units, and designating crypto reference officers or “ambassadors” to promote awareness and intelligence sharing. Raising awareness among senior management through targeted seminars may also help prioritize crypto asset enforcement within the agency’s broader mandate.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.111,
                0.62,
                0.885,
                0.727
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "Investing in analytical capabilities is critical. In the domain of crypto assets, revenue administration could explore partnerships with international and domestic stakeholders to advance data analytics applications specific to crypto assets, leveraging existing data sources and integrating blockchain analysis software. Experimentation with emerging technologies and data-driven approaches would enable more effective detection of undeclared mining, money mule schemes, and trade-based illicit financial flows.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.112,
                0.734,
                0.879,
                0.842
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "Developing analytical work on the use of crypto assets for tax evasion and customs fraud would be beneficial for the whole community of law enforcement agencies, as the current state of knowledge related to crypto asset fraud is still mainly focused on scams, thefts or use of cryptocurrencies on the Darkweb. Producing knowledge, based on fieldwork and analysis of real cases addressed by revenue administration, would raise the awareness of the crypto ecosystem on the misuses of crypto assets for tax and customs fraud.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.112,
                0.848,
                0.874,
                0.884
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "Finally, developing comprehensive training materials and expanding the use of open-source intelligence tools would further empower investigators to keep pace with the rapidly evolving crypto asset landscape.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "page_number",
            "bbox": [
                0.116,
                0.961,
                0.151,
                0.976
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "IMF"
        },
